### Step 1: Determine the Final Temperature ($T_{final}$)

The system consists of 1.0 lbm of ice at $32^\circ\text{F}$ and 6.0 lbm of water at $80^\circ\text{F}$. The system is adiabatic ($Q=0$) and operates at constant atmospheric pressure. We assume the final state is entirely liquid water (since the amount of hot water is significant compared to the ice).

The energy balance equation equates the energy required to melt the ice and raise its temperature to the energy released by the cooling water:
$$ \text{Energy Absorbed} = \text{Energy Released} $$
